      "text": "Bogotá to Cartagena"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:5a8704e80dc128a8",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "da7f2d251ea6877c963af975b1a5b276ae52991910b002e62c8f2f1dbd8c1840",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261110-tsvc722k5p",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, transfer to the airport for your flight to Cartagena de Indias. On arrival, we'll meet you, take you to your hotel in the chosen category and help you check in.\n\nAfter a rest, explore the city with an English-speaking guide. The Spanish founded Cartagena in 1533. It became a major port for shipping valuables from the colonies, and the city was protected by massive walls, forts, towers and stone bastions.\n\nYou'll see the old town, Catholic churches and convents, the Palace of the Inquisition and colonial mansions with balconies. One of the main fortresses is San Felipe, a major Spanish-era fortification. After the tour, return to your hotel."
    },
